    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling matchups against soft-tossing righties. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) headlines our lineup, carrying the highest efficiency score of the day as he faces Gallen; his 19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s xERA makes him an essential anchor in the heart of our order. **Trevor Story** (73.82) is our second-most explosive play, benefiting from a favorable wind-out projection and a prime matchup against Johnson, R. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (68.53) and **James Wood** (67.81) offer substantial upside. **James Wood** is particularly intriguing; despite facing a capable Buehler, his elite 0.419 xwOBA provides a high floor, while **Mickey Moniak** capitalizes on a strong dynamic platoon edge that effectively pushes him into \"Strong\" start territory.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today was **Cole Young**, who just missed the cut with a 51.76 score. While his matchup against Bradford is technically favorable due to the opponent's high xERA, he is relegated to the bottom of the order, which suppressed his run-scoring probability compared to the established veterans in our UTIL and MI slots. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki** (45.59); he is our riskiest start, as his production is significantly dampened by a 19% penalty against Henderson\u2019s specific arm profile. We are also wary of **Jose Caballero** (55.35); while he remains a vital cog for our stolen base scarcity, his 8th-hole placement and a negative dynamic platoon split against Sugano make him a marginal play that we are starting primarily for his speed-tool utility. No other major weather concerns are currently impacting the roster, though managers should monitor lineups for **Giancarlo Stanton** or **Tyler Soderstrom** updates should any late-scratch contingencies arise for the outfield or catcher slots.",
